Q28. Round Robin (RR)

Consider a Round Robin scheduler with a quantum of 3 time units.

| Job | Arrival time | CPU length |
| --- | ------------ | ---------- |
| A   | 0            | 7          |
| B   | 1            | 4          |
| C   | 4            | 2          |
| D   | 10           | 3          |

1. Write a scheduling trace showing every execution interval.
2. After each quantum expires, state the contents of the ready queue.
3. Calculate the completion time of each job.
4. Calculate the average turnaround time.
5. Calculate the average response time.
6. Explain what happens if a process finishes before exhausting its quantum.

New arrivals join the back of the ready queue; a process whose quantum expires is requeued at the back if it still has work remaining. There is no context-switch overhead.

